    <tags>dubbingmate youtube dubbing tts subtitles text-to-speech desktop</tags>
    <summary>Desktop app that reads YouTube subtitles aloud as speech in the language you choose.</summary>
    <description>DubbingMate is a desktop app (Windows and macOS) that turns the subtitles of a YouTube video into synthesized speech in the language you pick, so you can listen instead of reading. You can adjust the balance between the original audio and the dubbed voice.

## Licensing

DubbingMate is commercial software. The first dubbing starts a 72-hour free trial, with no card required. After the trial, continued use needs a one-time purchase (a license key for up to 3 devices, no subscription). Details are at https://dubbingmate.com.

## Package notes

* The package downloads the official installer from dubbingmate.com and checks its SHA256 checksum.
* The installer is an NSIS installer that is not code signed, so Windows SmartScreen may show a warning.
* Silent install uses the /S switch. Installation is per user (no administrator rights needed).
* Privacy policy: https://dubbingmate.com/privacy/
</description>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
